WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.919
Right now, as you're sitting here

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:06.240
watching my video, you can't feel your

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:08.480
organs moving inside your body, but they

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.719
are. Your stomach, intestines, lungs,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.639
everything is jiggling with every breath

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:15.360
and every body movement, but your brain

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:17.279
decided that's gross and irrelevant. So,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.800
it filtered it out. In fact, your brain

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:20.800
deletes millions of pieces of

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.800
information every day because it decided

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.119
on your behalf that it's not important

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.439
to you. So, what else is it hiding? What

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:29.279
if the opportunities, relationships, the

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:31.039
answers that you're looking for is all

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.960
right in front of you, but your brain

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:33.920
decided that it's not important? By the

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.760
end of this video, you're going to

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.280
understand exactly how this filter

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.960
works, why you notice the things that

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.200
you don't actually want to notice, and

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.840
how to reset that brain filter of yours

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.320
in the next 24 hours by tricking it and

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.320
playing a game where you tell your brain

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.399
exactly what you want to notice. My name

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.320
is May. My community is called Stoic

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:54.000
Angels. And on this channel, we do the

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.760
full work. We work on our brains, our

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.239
beauty, our aura so that we can

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.160
restructure how we think, how we feel in

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:01.680
our bodies, and how we show up in the

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.760
world. If that's what you're here for,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.080
subscribe because we go deep every

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.080
single week.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.799
There's a system in your brain stem

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:13.439
called the reticular activating system,

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:16.000
the RA. Your brain processes millions of

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:18.720
bits of information per second, but you

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.479
can only consciously perceive about 50,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.880
which to be honest is still pretty

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.479
impressive to me. So the re decides what

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.720
gets through and what gets deleted and

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:28.560
it makes that decision based on what you

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.320
tell your brain is important to you. For

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.920
example, let's say you want a new car.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.840
Suddenly you're going to see this car

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.680
everywhere. It has always been there,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.119
but your brain just started noticing it

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.119
through this filter. [music] So if you

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:40.799
spend the last year focused on all of

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.880
your problems, talking about your

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:44.960
problems, complaining about it. What has

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.200
your brain been filtering out? What kind

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.119
of opportunities did your brain miss out

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.040
on because it didn't match the filter

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:53.520
that you set in it, which might even be

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.200
why is everything so hard? Especially if

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.360
you complain about it. Your everyday

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.280
thoughts happen to you quickly and

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.000
almost impossible to catch actually. But

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.320
your speech comparatively is slower and

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.360
more limited in that it's physical. But

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.440
then your speech is also how you express

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:11.440
your inner world to the outer world. So

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.621
what if we start to focus on this

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.280
bridge? That is exactly the point

00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:18.000
[music] when your brain filter becomes

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.440
an expression of who you are. So if you

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.360
say things like things never work out

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.800
for me, everything is always so hard,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.599
more than it should be, you're giving

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.680
your an instruction to look for even

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:29.599
more evidence that things indeed [music]

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.720
do not work out for you. So that's what

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:32.400
it would do. Or to give you more

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.480
examples, when you say things like, "Oh,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.560
I'm so behind." Or, "I can't afford

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.640
this. This always happens to me." You're

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.800
not actually describing your reality,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.120
but your perception of it because you're

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.879
instructing your brain on what to keep

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.560
showing you. Even if you don't mean it,

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:47.920
you're telling it, "I want more of

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.440
this." So, let me tell you something

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.280
personal that happened to me a couple of

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.800
months ago. And this is absolutely not

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.640
the same thing because it's more so

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.239
about processing. And I wanted to give

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.519
you guys a very good example of it

00:02:56.239 --> 00:02:59.120
because I'd say something terrible

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:00.480
actually did happen to you. How do we

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.480
stop holding on to things that we don't

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.000
want anymore? How can we move on? So,

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.360
I'm going to bring this up and this is

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.519
maybe one of the last times I'll bring

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:10.000
it up. I found out that my biological

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:12.640
father had passed away and he had been

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.480
in a coma for a few years before that.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.560
Nobody came to visit him except for my

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.400
half brother's lawyer. And that lawyer

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.480
was there to basically see if he was

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.120
still alive or not. And this whole thing

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.760
is very vile. And I was estranged from

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.640
that entire side of my family for years

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.159
for extremely valid reasons. I literally

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.599
never wanted to speak to them ever again

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:33.120
because my life is so much better

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:35.360
without them in it. But yeah, I had to

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.440
find this out and I was horrified when I

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.920
found out what happened because it was

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.519
just really sad. But he was not a good

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.040
parent to me nor a good husband to my

00:03:41.519 --> 00:03:44.879
mom and my mom divorced him when I was

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.560
very young and we lost contact when I

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:48.080
moved to the States because I really had

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.879
to get away from it. And when I found

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.560
out what happened, it was a very messy

00:03:50.879 --> 00:03:54.720
feeling. It was extremely messy because

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.959
imagine trying to get closure from

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.879
something like that. And I had all of

00:03:56.959 --> 00:04:00.560
this unfinished business, like a

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:02.959
conversation that we were supposed to

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.439
have, but now we'll never have it ever.

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:07.760
And before he went into that coma, he

00:04:05.439 --> 00:04:09.760
actually left me a few voicemails, which

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.400
was sort of his attempt to reach out to

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.560
me. And he made a Facebook profile. He

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.720
had a photo up, and that photo is the

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.959
only photo that I have of him. And I've

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.799
never seen him as an older man before

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:23.040
with white hairs and all of that. So

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:25.280
that's when I realized that I have been

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.120
replaying these early childhood memories

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.840
of mine in my head over and over again

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.680
without properly processing it. And I've

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.600
just been carrying it around my entire

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.600
life without even noticing. So when you

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.000
carry these things with you, it becomes

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.560
a part of you, a part of your brain and

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.240
also a part of your RA. I'm currently

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.400
doing schema therapy with my

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.560
psychologist, my psych. And basically

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.560
what schemaotherapy is is that it's

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.800
about exploring your identity and the

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.880
core beliefs that you carry around about

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.560
who you are. A lot of these core beliefs

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.560
or core memories will form in your

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.560
childhood. And one of the techniques she

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.648
uses is called the empty chair where you

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.320
imagine someone sitting across you

00:05:00.648 --> 00:05:04.400
[music] and you get to say all of the

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.400
things you never got to say to them. So

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.000
before my therapist left for vacation,

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.560
she assigned this to me as a homework

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.479
and she said, "I want you to imagine

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.080
having a conversation with your father

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.600
between our sessions." And I swear this

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.800
is how things always work out in my life

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.560
because that's when I found the sponsor

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.160
of today's video which is called Vit.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.840
It's an app and when you first open this

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.680
app, there's a whole library of

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.440
characters already built in that you can

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.960
have real-time live video conversations

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.120
with. But what's so cool to me is that

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.199
you can make your own custom avatar like

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.960
the Sims. You can upload a photo. For

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:35.120
example, this is my cat. And it brings

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.960
them to life as a realtime video

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.199
conversation. You describe their

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.960
personality, their vibe, how they talk.

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:42.800
You can actually have a [music] live

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.320
video call with them like a FaceTime.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:46.240
This means they respond to you

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.080
immediately with facial expressions,

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.080
their voice, and they even have

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.320
long-term memory. So, they remember your

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:54.479
previous conversations. So, what I did

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.720
was I uploaded the only recent photo I

00:05:54.479 --> 00:05:58.320
have of my dad. It was what I found on

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:00.240
Facebook. Like I mentioned, I had never

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.160
seen him this old before. I described

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.479
his personality to the app and I said

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.400
the things that I really needed to say.

00:06:04.479 --> 00:06:09.440
Hearing him talk to me and having this

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.840
conversation that felt so long overdue

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.280
by over 20 years, even knowing that it

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.039
wasn't actually him because it's not

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.479
here anymore. Just something about it

00:06:15.039 --> 00:06:19.039
changed the way that I was sort of

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:21.199
carrying my emotional burdens. It gave

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:22.960
me a new perspective on my feelings I've

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:24.880
been carrying for years. Because the

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.800
empty chair technique works, but there's

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:29.280
something about it actually feeling like

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:32.319
a conversation rather than a monologue

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.479
into silence that makes my processing so

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:37.120
much deeper. You can even clone a voice

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:39.360
from a short recording. I kept my dad's

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.120
voicemails from years ago. I haven't

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.199
done this step yet, but maybe I'll try

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.520
it out later. And in the meantime, I

00:06:43.199 --> 00:06:48.479
also have my cat on VD program to tell

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:50.720
me about my daily schedule on my travel

00:06:48.479 --> 00:06:52.319
itinerary so I don't miss him too much

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.240
while I'm traveling. Although this is

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:56.000
not a replacement for therapy, it's a

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.680
great processing tool and I'll be

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.360
telling my therapist about how I did my

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.560
homework with Vi when she gets back. Try

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.560
it out in the download link in the

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.560
description.

00:07:04.639 --> 00:07:08.160
The thing about your problems is every

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:10.880
single one that you've ever had

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.919
eventually will pass or gets resolved or

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.599
you evolve past it. Problems are always

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:17.680
temporary. But complaining about it

00:07:15.599 --> 00:07:19.840
though, it freezes them in place and

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.840
reinforces it in your life. So when

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:23.440
you're complaining, you're taking this

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.120
problem that's already happening to you.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.639
Maybe it's even on the way out. It's

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.080
like you take a screenshot of it. You

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:29.599
send that screenshot to everyone you

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.520
know. You save it as your lock screen on

00:07:29.599 --> 00:07:33.120
your phone. And now you're staring at

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.880
this frozen image. Everyone that you've

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.560
spoken to has also seen the screenshot

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.759
or if you post about it on social media.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.759
Guess what? You're going to get reminded

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:41.680
of it with every comment and every like

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:43.440
that you get. Every time you retell your

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.120
story, you're pulling the problem back

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.639
from the edge of it going away and

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.560
you're basically being like, "No, no,

00:07:46.639 --> 00:07:50.800
no, no. Stay here. I want to hold on to

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.800
you." So, if you think about it, has

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.560
complaining actually ever helped you

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.520
with your situation? What it does

00:07:54.560 --> 00:08:00.160
instead is it gives you the sensation of

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:02.319
having taken action on something without

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.560
actually doing anything. This is also

00:08:02.319 --> 00:08:06.879
why I always encourage people like don't

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.960
tell anyone about your grand huge

00:08:06.879 --> 00:08:11.039
projects until you're almost done with

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:13.520
it or when it's pretty much done because

00:08:11.039 --> 00:08:15.360
it stops you from even working on it in

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.520
the first place. Your brain already got

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.680
their dopamine hit. So then there's no

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.520
more incentive to do the work. And

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.759
there's a difference between processing

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:25.440
your emotions and performing it. And

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:28.080
what complaining is is that it's a

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.080
performance. Processing has an end goal.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:32.320
I felt hurt by what happened. I'm going

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:34.560
to work through it. But a performance

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.719
though, it's a loop. That means I'm

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.560
telling all four of my besties what

00:08:36.719 --> 00:08:40.399
happened when I broke up with soand so

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.240
and whatever. And every time you tell

00:08:40.399 --> 00:08:44.240
it, that's like the last thing that your

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.600
besties will remember you by. And then

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.120
every time they see you, they're going

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:49.040
to be like, "Oh, hey, what happened?

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.279
How's it going? How are you feeling from

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:53.600
the breakup?" Even when you're totally

00:08:51.279 --> 00:08:55.440
over it, that still brings it back. It

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.440
reinforces the problem. But what if your

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.440
problems are not here to punish you? But

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.519
they are here for you to redirect them.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:03.440
Think about it like a GPS. You're

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:06.000
driving towards something and the road

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:07.600
closes. You have two choices. You pull

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.040
over and you call everyone you know. You

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.440
tell everyone how unfair this road

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.519
closure is, or you take another path.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.440
Sometimes this reroute takes you

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:16.880
someplace even better. You may even find

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:18.959
a shortcut that you didn't even know

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.880
exist and you may not even have found it

00:09:18.959 --> 00:09:22.560
out if the original road hadn't closed

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:24.000
in the first place. So when you reroute

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:26.399
your problems that way, every time you

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.920
encounter an issue, it's not a problem

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.360
because you know it's going to go away.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.519
It's not a dead end. They are just

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:33.440
simply course corrections. So the sooner

00:09:31.519 --> 00:09:36.000
you stop complaining about this closed

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.680
road and start rerouting yourself, the

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:40.240
faster you will actually arrive

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:42.080
someplace you want to be. Your RA is

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.480
either set to look for more evidence

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:46.640
that this road is in fact closed when

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.880
you already knew this or look for the

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:50.560
new route. You choose by what you speak

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.920
and whether you treat your problems as

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.920
your destination or a detour.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.399
So if you ask me May, how do I stop

00:09:58.399 --> 00:10:02.560
obsessing over this thing that I don't

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:04.399
want and actually redirect my focus to

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.480
something I do want? How can I work on

00:10:04.399 --> 00:10:08.800
myself better and think about my success

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:10.800
like all the time? So, here's a fun way

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:11.839
to reset this filter in your brain.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:13.839
Basically, we're going to play a trick

00:10:11.839 --> 00:10:16.160
on our brains by playing a game with it.

00:10:13.839 --> 00:10:18.240
Our brain may need to gify stuff to make

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.880
it more, you know, absorbable. So, for

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:23.519
the next 24 hours, say this sentence out

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.360
loud. Brain, show me proof that

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:28.000
everything in my life is here to help

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:30.240
me. Or you can replace that with the

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.560
universe or God, whatever you believe

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.040
in. But that's the instruction. You're

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:37.120
giving your RA a new criteria for the

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.880
filter and you're saying it out loud

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:40.959
with your words. And then when you place

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:43.200
your head in that direction, the actual

00:10:40.959 --> 00:10:45.600
game is to collect various things that

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.920
happened to you for the next 24 hours or

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:50.399
things that you notice that prove you're

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.640
indeed being supported. And they must be

00:10:50.399 --> 00:10:55.760
tiny little things like for example, you

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:58.079
go outside, you see 10 dogs or a problem

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:59.920
that you have suddenly resolves itself.

00:10:58.079 --> 00:11:01.920
Or if you want to get even more specific

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:04.320
and you tell your brain, brain, I want

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:06.240
to see 10 red cars when I go outside for

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:08.560
a walk in an hour. And then you go

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.880
outside for a walk and count how many

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:13.200
red cars you see. You can be as specific

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.040
or as general as you want. And if you

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.800
want something to track this with, I

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.120
made a free PDF guide for this

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.560
experiment talking about it in detail.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.560
It's in the description. So go and

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:24.480
download it. It has the game rules and

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:26.399
evidence tracker so you can write down

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:28.160
everything that your brain finds for you

00:11:26.399 --> 00:11:29.680
over the next 24 hours. And I'm going to

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.600
put some additional studies in there as

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:33.839
well. But basically, every time it

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.480
happens, say to yourself or write it

00:11:33.839 --> 00:11:38.959
down, that's evidence. Evidence that

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:40.959
things are indeed going the way that you

00:11:38.959 --> 00:11:43.279
want it to. Because here's what happens

00:11:40.959 --> 00:11:44.959
in your brain. Every time you notice and

00:11:43.279 --> 00:11:47.120
acknowledge a piece of evidence, you are

00:11:44.959 --> 00:11:49.519
reinforcing the new filter. Your brain

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:51.839
starts to scan for evidence. This plays

00:11:49.519 --> 00:11:54.240
a huge role in a lot of the things that

00:11:51.839 --> 00:11:56.480
we work on. Things like gratitude

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.560
practices. Why is being grateful so

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.640
transformative and why does it help us

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.480
so much? This is the same type of

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:04.720
compounding effect. If you want to focus

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:07.040
on gratitude or whatever you want to

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:08.880
focus on, the filter in your brain

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.880
starts to change. And once your mind

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.639
starts noticing new things, you get new

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.560
thoughts or even your existing actions

00:12:12.639 --> 00:12:16.240
may start to change as a result. And

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:19.279
once the things that you start doing

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:21.920
changes, your reality changes. It's

00:12:19.279 --> 00:12:23.839
almost inevitable that it does. This

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:26.880
isn't even magical thinking. It's a

00:12:23.839 --> 00:12:28.880
basic feedback loop. It's so logical.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.399
And every time you reinforce something

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:32.480
that you don't want by putting it out

00:12:30.399 --> 00:12:34.880
there, you're making it work against

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.959
you. But now that you know that you can

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:39.360
in fact trick your brain to do whatever

00:12:36.959 --> 00:12:42.480
you want, you get to use it in your

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.839
favor. So try this out for 24 hours and

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.760
you will start to see new things that

00:12:43.839 --> 00:12:48.079
your brain used to just ignore. And

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.920
obviously make sure that if you're being

00:12:48.079 --> 00:12:52.000
specific about it that it's still within

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:54.000
the realm of possibility. You're not

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.920
asking your brain to move a mountain for

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.839
you. For example, don't ask your brain

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.680
to show you 10 red cars when you're at a

00:12:57.839 --> 00:13:01.600
place where there aren't even any cars

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:03.440
or no cars are allowed. Then that won't

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:05.120
even make sense and you basically are

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.959
just setting yourself up for failure.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:08.560
You know what I'm saying? Don't sabotage

00:13:06.959 --> 00:13:10.720
yourself. You have got to make it very

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.079
easy for your brain to deliver the

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.399
evidence to you. And you're going to see

00:13:12.079 --> 00:13:16.079
what I'm talking about. The reason why I

00:13:14.399 --> 00:13:18.560
bring up the story about my biological

00:13:16.079 --> 00:13:21.040
